                    "a": "Title: Live for Others\nPrécis: Like trees, which stand in the sun and endure heat yet give shade and fruit for the benefit of others, a good man lives for others. Sandalwood yields more scent when rubbed, and sugarcane gives more juice when cut into pieces. Whether people praise him or not, and whether he lives long or dies soon, he who treads the right path never leaves it. Life is unprofitable if it is not lived for others; to live only for oneself is to live a purposeless life.",
                    "q": "Write the précis of the following paragraph and suggest a suitable title: 'Trees give shade for the benefit of others, and while they themselves stand in the sun and endure the heat, they produce the fruit of which others profit. The character of good human is like that of trees. Sandalwood, the more it is rubbed, the more scent does it yield. Sugarcane, the more it is peeled and cut up into pieces, the more juice does it produce. What matters whether other people praise them or not? What difference does it make whether they die at this moment or whether lives are prolonged? Happen what may, those who tread in the right path will not set foot in any other. Life itself is unprofitable to a human being who does not live for others. To live for the mere sake of living one's life is to live the life with no purpose.'"
