                    "a": "Model speech: Respected principal, honourable teachers and dear fellow students, Assalam-o-Alaikum. Today I am going to speak on the topic: 'To empower women with education is to empower the Nation'. Education is the light that removes the darkness of ignorance. When we educate a woman, we educate a whole family, because a mother is the first teacher of her children. An educated woman can raise healthy, educated children, manage her home wisely, and take part in the progress of the country. Our religion also teaches us that seeking knowledge is the duty of every Muslim man and woman. In Pakistan, great women like Fatima Jinnah, Benazir Bhutto and Malala Yousafzai have shown what an educated woman can achieve. Yet many girls in our villages still cannot go to school because of poverty and old customs. We must change this. Let us promise today that we will send every girl to school, because to empower women with education is to empower the nation. Thank you. (Model answer.)",
