                    "a": "Compound-complex — two main clauses joined by 'but' ('I had a beautiful plant by my window' / 'it died') plus the dependent clause 'since I forgot to water it regularly'. (Note: the book's table lists only Simple, Compound and Complex; this sentence has both a compound and a complex structure.)",
