                    "a": "Lucy's parents went shouting far and wide all that night, but there was neither sound nor sight to guide them. At day-break they stood on a hill overlooking the moor and saw the wooden bridge a furlong from their door. Then they tracked her small footmarks downwards from the steep hill's edge, through the broken hawthorn hedge and by the long stone-wall, across an open field, and to the bridge — where the footmarks went into the middle of the plank and further there were none.",
                    "q": "7. What efforts did Lucy's parents make in finding her?"
