                    "a": "Henri René Albert Guy de Maupassant (1850–1893) was a 19th-century French author, remembered as a master of the short story. He wrote 300 short stories, six novels, three travel books and one volume of verse. His first published story, 'Boule de Suif', is often considered his masterpiece. His stories are second only to Shakespeare's in their inspiration of movie adaptations.",
