                "q": "1. Select the correct option.\n(i) For any complex number z, |z| is equal to\n(a) |z̄|\n(b) |-z|\n(c) |-z̄|\n(d) All of these\n(ii) If z_1 and z_2 are any two complex numbers, then\n(a) |z_1 + z_2| < |z_1| + |z_2|\n(b) |z_1 + z_2| ≤ |z_1| + |z_2|\n(c) |z_1 - z_2| < |z_1| - |z_2|\n(d) |z_1 + z_2| ≥ |z_1| + |z_2|\n(iii) If z = 3i - 4, then z + z̄ = --------\n(a) 8\n(b) -3i\n(c) -8\n(d) 3i - 8\n(iv) If a > 0 and b < 0 then\n(a) ab > 0\n(b) ab < 0\n(c) ab = 0\n(d) All of these\n(v) If n is an even integer, then (i)^n is equal to:\n(a) i\n(b) -i\n(c) 1 or -1\n(d) i or -i\n(vi) If z is any real number x, then its conjugate is:\n(a) x\n(b) -x\n(c) xi\n(d) -xi\n(vii) (-1)^(-21/2) is equal to:\n(a) i\n(b) -i\n(c) 1\n(d) -1\n(viii) If z = (0, 1) then z^2 is:\n(a) 1\n(b) -1\n(c) i\n(d) -i\n(ix) The product of two conjugate complex numbers is:\n(a) A real number\n(b) An imaginary number\n(c) Always zero\n(d) A complex number\n(x) Real part of (2 + i)/i is equal to:\n(a) 1\n(b) 2\n(c) -1\n(d) 1/2\n(xi) The plane on which complex numbers are reprsented is called:\n(a) Coordinate plane\n(b) Complex plane\n(c) Cartesian plane\n(d) Real plane\n(xii) The modulus of a complex number z = x + iy is the distance of P(x, y) from:\n(a) x - axis\n(b) y - axis\n(c) Origin\n(d) (x, y)\n(xiii) If z_1 = 2 + 3i, z_2 = 1 - i then |z_1 z_2| = ------------\n(a) √13\n(b) √26\n(c) √15\n(d) 26\n(xiv) If |x + 5i| = 3, then x is equal to:\n(a) ±4\n(b) ±4i\n(c) ±22i\n(d) None of these\n(xv) Multiplicative inverse of (3, 4) is:\n(a) (3/25, 4/25)\n(b) (3/25, -4/25)\n(c) (-3/25, -4/25)\n(d) (1, 0)\n(xvi) If z = -3i + 4, then z̄ = ------------\n(a) -3i - 4\n(b) -3i + 4\n(c) 3i + 4\n(d) 3i - 4\n(xvii) Real and imaginary part of i(3 - 2i) are respectively:\n(a) 2 & -3\n(b) 2 & 3\n(c) 3 & -2\n(d) -3 & -2\n(xviii) If z = a + ib, then |z| =: ------------\n(a) √(a - b)\n(b) √(a^2 - b^2)\n(c) √(a^2 + b^2)\n(d) √(a - b)\n(xix) ((1 + i)/(1 - i))^12 = ------------\n(a) -1\n(b) 1\n(c) i\n(d) -i\n(xx) The value of i^-7 is: ------------\n(a) 1\n(b) i\n(c) -1\n(d) -i"
