                    "a": "[[T]]Feature|Cartilaginous fishes (Chondrichthyes)|Bony fishes (Osteichthyes)\nEndoskeleton| Made of cartilage rather than bone| Bony\nExoskeleton| Enormous number of tiny sharp enamel-coated denticles called placoid scales| Tiny bony plates called cycloid or ctenoid scales, according to whether their outer edge is smooth or spiny\nMouth| Ventral in position| At the anterior tip\nGills| Usually 5 exposed gill slits on the side, not covered by a gill cover (operculum)| Covered over on each side by a gill cover called the operculum\nTail fin| Heterocercal| Usually homocercal or diphycercal\nAir bladder| Absent| Present in most, acting as a hydrostatic organ\nExamples| Sharks, skates and rays; Scoliodon (dog fish) is a small shark common in our seas| Eel, sea horse, flying fish, globe fish, pomfret and carps (rahu)[[/T]]",
                    "q": "5. Differentiate between cartilaginous fishes and bony fishes"
