                    "q": "2. Ammonia gas can be produced by heating together the solid NH4Cl and Ca(OH)2.\n2NH4Cl + Ca(OH)2 → 2NH3 + CaCl2 + 2H2O\nIf a mixture containing 100g of each of these solids is heated, determine the limiting reactant and the mass of NH3 gas produced."
