                    "a": "Given: rate of pumping = 500 gram/minute = 0.5 kg/minute, height h = 120 m, efficiency = 50%, g = 9.8 m/s^2\nMass pumped per second = 0.5/60 kg/s = 0.00833 kg/s\nOutput power = (mass per second) × g × h\nP_out = 0.00833 × 9.8 × 120\nP_out = 9.8 W\nEfficiency = P_out / P_in\n0.5 = 9.8 / P_in\nP_in = 9.8 / 0.5\nP_in = 19.6 W\nP_in = 20 Watt",
                    "q": "11. A motor pumps the water at the rate 500 gram/minute to the height of 120 m. If the motor is 50% efficient then how much input electric power is needed? (Ans: 20 watt)"
