                    "a": "Given: total cross-sectional area of the major arteries A = 2.1 cm^2\nFrom Worked Example 7.3 in the book, the volume rate of blood flow in the aorta is:\nRadius of aorta r = 1.2 cm, speed of blood in the aorta v = 40 cm/s\nArea of aorta A_aorta = πr^2 = 3.14 × (1.2)^2 = 4.52 cm^2\nVolume rate of flow Q = A_aorta × v = 4.52 × 40 = 181 cm^3/s\nBy the equation of continuity, the same volume rate flows through the major arteries:\nAverage speed v = Q/A\nv = 181 / 2.1\nv = 86 cm/s\n(Note: the book gives 13.6 cm/s, but that value does not follow from the data of Example 7.3 in the chapter; using the example's data the speed is 86 cm/s.)",
